- op: discuss  # 5e9d
  at: '2026-06-02T07:33:27Z'  # 5e9d
  by: agent  # 5e9d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5e9d
  clock: 4  # 5e9d
  nonce: 5e9d  # 5e9d
  message: "Pass-31 face: verify-claims YAML silently accepts unrecognized fields, producing \"inconclusive\" verdict that consumers may misread as \"the constraint was checked\" (F31.4).\n\n**Existing INV-fabov scope** lists \"a verification subcommand silently accepting unknown constraint types and unknown taint flag values.\" Pass-31 documents the specific cost: the Phase 3 PR4 fix that closed silent-CONFIRM (ClaimVerdict.inconclusive shipping) inadvertently introduced silent-INCONCLUSIVE-on-typo as a residual face.\n\n**Test sequence.** Four YAMLs filed against substrate at `/tmp/hg-dogfood-s21/bm.json`:\n\n```\n# Variant 1 — used `kind: must_exist`, `pattern:`, `description:` (all unrecognized)\nverdict=inconclusive, \"No machine-checkable constraint on this claim.\"\n\n# Variant 2 — used `kind: must_not_reach`, `from:`, `to:`, `matching:` (all unrecognized)\nverdict=inconclusive, same message.\n\n# Variant 3 — used `kind: must_exist`, `constraint.{kind, language, min_count}` (mostly unrecognized)\nverdict=inconclusive, same message.\n\n# Variant 4 — used `constraint.{boundary, must_not_exist}` and `constraint.{boundary, max_chains}` (recognized)\nverdict=violated, evidence_count=10 (net_send) / 152 (subprocess), correct.\n```\n\nThe verdict \"inconclusive — No machine-checkable constraint on this claim\" appears whether (a) the YAML is structurally correct but the constraint genuinely lacks a checker (correct), or (b) the YAML has typos / unrecognized fields making the constraint silently dropped at parse time (incorrect — should warn).\n\n**Consumer impact.** A security analyst writing `constrant.must_not_exist` (typo) or `constraint.must-not-exist` (wrong key style) or `kind: must_exist` (uses spec-narrative wording that doesn't map to load_claims() at verify_claims.py:218-225) gets \"inconclusive\" and may believe the claim was correctly parsed but not implemented. The fix that closed INV-bitig (silent-confirm) introduced this new face — silent-inconclusive — at the verify-claims YAML parsing layer.\n\n**Verify-claims load_claims() at lines 188-228** does `entry.get(\"id\", \"\")`, `entry.get(\"text\", \"\")`, `constraint.get(\"boundary\", \"\")`, `constraint.get(\"must_not_exist\", False)`, etc. There's no validation that all keys in `entry` or `constraint` are recognized; unknown keys are silently ignored. The Claim dataclass populates from these gets and proceeds.\n\n**Fix-path candidates** (within existing INV-fabov scope):\n1. Reject unknown top-level fields in claim entries with `KeyError`/`ValueError` at load time.\n2. Reject unknown sub-fields of `constraint` similarly.\n3. Add a `schema_version` check that fails on unknown version (currently `schema_version: 1` is the loader's expectation but unrecognized values aren't rejected).\n4. Emit a warning when load_claims sees keys outside the recognized set and the resulting Claim is \"empty\" of recognized constraints.\n\nSame root pattern as INV-fabov's catalogued symptoms (\"a verification subcommand silently accepting unknown constraint types\"). Pass-31 supplies the worked-example sequence demonstrating the silent-acceptance behavior with concrete invalid YAMLs.\n\nNo status change. Pass-31 supplies a verify-claims face for INV-fabov demonstrating that the Phase 3 silent-confirm closure left silent-inconclusive open.\n\nProbe artifact: pass-31 probe C — 4 progressively-correct claim YAMLs in /tmp/p31_claims*.yaml."  # 5e9d
